 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 545229,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the four apportionment methods discussed in this section is biased toward states with smaller populations?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>The Adams method.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Adams’s method favors smaller states. One of the Your Turn exercises showed this tendency. Here is a reminder:</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>&nbsp;</th>\n<th>Standard Divisor: 11,500</th>\n<th>&nbsp;</th>\n<th>Divisor: 12,000</th>\n<th>&nbsp;</th>\n<th>Divisor: 12,500</th>\n<th>&nbsp;</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Modified Quota</td>\n<td>Upper Quota</td>\n<td>Modified Quota</td>\n<td>Upper Quota</td>\n<td>Modified Quota</td>\n<td>Upper Quota</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>0.87</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>0.83</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>0.8</td>\n<td>1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>B</td>\n<td>8.7</td>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>8.33</td>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>8</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>C</td>\n<td>86.96</td>\n<td>87</td>\n<td>83.33</td>\n<td>84</td>\n<td>80</td>\n<td>80</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The first change from 11,500 to 12,000:</p>\n<p>States A and B had no change.</p>\n<p>State C lost 3.</p>\n<p>The second change from 12,000 to 12,500:</p>\n<p>State A lost nothing.</p>\n<p>State B lost 1.</p>\n<p>State C lost 4.</p>\n<p>Overall, state C had the greatest losses each time the divisor was increased.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
